#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230002} :activity/id #uuid "bb024668-aa54-5547-86a8-56f97596b95b" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230002 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230188 :tutorial/content "Matrix exponentials can be used for solving homogeneous systems of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix.\n\nFor example, consider the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-5x(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/f9/f94140f8c9fe736ca7c574547658856e85d938eb08064046716be8eb1a2748de.svg)\nwhere ![](images/26/26dcf2c367c915460d09f4f38b40e4f792a06b6ab44291b4739a6935529daf89.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/90/9000e03ddf617a1e3c4e0eed5da2b846d62e3d68588b601d90643783960d17df.svg)\n\nRecall that given the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is some constant vector.\n\nSince we have already seen how to compute the standard fundamental matrix, we will not repeat the calculation here. So, computing the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system, we get\n![](images/11/11e0da79656b7f8e2c84c6c54e6dd6b54cf53cbb8e746d44dfb13329c3d2ed8f.svg)\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.$\n\n**Note:** Recall that for the general solution of the ordinary differential equation $x'(t)=ax(t),$ we have \n\n$$\nx'(t)=ax(t)\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nx(t) = c \\, e^{at}, \n\\quad\nc \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nNow, for the general solution of the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n\\quad\n\\mathbf{c} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n.\n$$\n\nLet's see more examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "978fc2f4-910c-5bef-9ae3-3da9377642ce" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14515 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "c774d65b-c500-58e4-aa9a-e222d3d136ae" :step/math-academy-id 592270 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230003}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230003 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228910 :question/id #uuid "26df399d-cd87-5b5d-9f3f-7ced4ca5fd06" :question/math-academy-id "e-21707"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5bc609b-dc5b-52e9-9f0e-206f32bb829b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050125} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050228}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229669} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229677} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308684} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308685} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402113} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445608} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445610} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445613} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542220} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555759} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563755}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Homogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"} :step/id #uuid "d3b52974-38d7-50fa-b648-b51510a9a617" :step/math-academy-id 592271 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230004}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230004 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230193 :tutorial/content "Now, let's find the solution to the initial value problem below\n![](images/31/3111f065d441881e050417b345b34947509f175f00ebd5402963e432d013348e.svg)\n\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/5c/5c4ed0a2e9db0979e4fc0342c2e4db7c23c60cf58293a496fa661ff1c03fccde.svg)\nwhere ![](images/71/7164659247c5290544655b05943d7d998f67cb1cc3b4cc45bab0902e8059bc75.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/e3/e3f94e8ce2cc2063d469fbac2af87232cc130f788243c1507bfe9972dd4b04c1.svg)\n\nRecall that the general solution of the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is some constant vector.\n\nEvaluating both sides of $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} \\mathbf{c}$ at $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c \\\\ x(0) & ={e}^{A(0)}\\,c \\\\ x(0) & =I\\,c \\\\ c & =x(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to our initial value problem is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{x}(0).\n$$\n\nComputing the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system, we get\n![](images/fc/fc4e1ba16be420fbe5e53e2dbb4ee6da96c7097bbe4e117315407ec4dc65365f.svg)\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{7t} & t{e}^{7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(3-2t){e}^{7t} \\\\ -2{e}^{7t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "9cb11887-9535-5a54-a180-eb20a7534696" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14529 :tutorial/title "Solving Initial Value Problems"} :step/id #uuid "5206e604-fe74-5b8a-800c-cdb747dc1e28" :step/math-academy-id 592274 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230005}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230005 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228918 :question/id #uuid "ead811e0-8551-5b15-8b49-711cbe0b8498" :question/math-academy-id "e-21725"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229657} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229682} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308537} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311559} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311560} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311561} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311562} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311563} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372698} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372703} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445609} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445611} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482598} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555774}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"} :step/id #uuid "c93fbf09-3c42-5a66-8e76-1cf0d810f44a" :step/math-academy-id 592275 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230006}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230006 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230194 :tutorial/content "Next, let's find the solution to the initial value problem \n![](images/93/93f9c58b8a9cea64ba97f43f2831336ea8d38a6fd6165211a54d2822415c1497.svg)\ngiven that ![](images/ee/ee25228bf71d1b7d9d0688af06a7f1335c252310127b403ed0ed37f7fe277c07.svg) where ![](images/3a/3a3ac9326741c0e2390a8e2f079808f0b432b740149ef4b034ffa7568dc33848.svg)\n\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/2b/2b81cf358ffb3df49f327b63138640ac452a249f989353b521be34d531aeffd9.svg)\nwhere ![](images/11/1110f0bdbe784b21683bfb9610ca9c04e5a45755954d49a15124e530feef2002.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/47/47d8a0214e5ccdf6625a330d23003dec11cbc3a4f35cb2992df29a688963e4b2.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution is $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c}.$ We can determine the constant vector $\\mathbf{c}$ using the initial condition at time $t=t_0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0) = e^{At_0} \\, \\mathbf{c} \\implies \\mathbf{c} = e^{-At_0} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nsince the inverse of $e^{At_0}$ is $e^{-At_0}.$ Plugging this back into our general solution gives the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our specific problem (with $t_0=1$) is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-1)) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "0fe9a975-9d92-5f79-8a67-34af55196fb3" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14530 :tutorial/title "Solving Initial Value Problems With Shifted Conditions"} :step/id #uuid "19b34f7c-755c-5e1b-a16f-22bd17d1ecc7" :step/math-academy-id 592278 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230007}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230007 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228917 :question/id #uuid "b061f2b1-b015-582f-921f-9b444db631ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-21723"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229664} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229684} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311564} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311590} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311591} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311592} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311593} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311594} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391579} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391586} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445615} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482582} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555867} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563702}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"} :step/id #uuid "633a401e-5116-5c9e-a0b4-8848cf596d7b" :step/math-academy-id 592279 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230008}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230008 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230192 :tutorial/content "Before proceeding with the next example, let's recall some important properties of matrix exponentials:\n\n1\\. *Law of Exponents:* If $A$ is a constant square matrix, then\n\n  $$\n  e^{A(t+s)} = e^{At}\\,e^{As}.\n  $$\n\n2\\. *Inverse:* For any $t,$ the matrix $e^{At}$ is invertible and \n\n  $$\n  (e^{At})^{-1} = e^{-At}.\n  $$\n\n3\\. *Identity:* For any square matrix $A,$\n\n  $$\n  e^{A\\cdot 0} = I.\n  $$\n\n4\\. *Product of exponentials:* If $A$ and $B$ commute (i.e., $AB = BA$), then\n\n  $$\n  e^{A}e^{B} = e^{A+B}.\n  $$\n\n  **Watch out!** In general, this identity is *not true* unless $A$ and $B$ commute.\n\nLet's see how these properties can be used in practice." :tutorial/id #uuid "5ae3cfa7-a5a5-5a50-aefa-8b8dec561567" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14528 :tutorial/title "Reminder: Properties of Matrix Exponentials"} :step/id #uuid "eb56047e-3845-5f8e-9282-d41f308270e3" :step/math-academy-id 592282 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230009}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230009 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228911 :question/id #uuid "ace067cd-e1d0-5b3e-bae2-bf58dcac3585" :question/math-academy-id "e-21711"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229658} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229697} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311712} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311794} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311799} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372710} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396936} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396993} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445612} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445614} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482509} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482614}] :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"} :step/id #uuid "6a90e198-ec80-5daf-8cb9-69841a16a32d" :step/math-academy-id 592283}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186229256}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482627} :activity/id #uuid "14357ccb-7387-5d90-95d5-9ec0c77cd805" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482627 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482598 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c9df7eb-dd1e-53e0-a87d-68b6fd1f480c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481800} {:answer/id #uuid "b3959273-da78-54bd-9652-5e91ff910d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482197} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf2cf7c-d4c9-58ad-ac1c-f6f73d55b4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482226} {:answer/id #uuid "c6299321-746c-562a-a610-1a2b40cd8433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482243} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfaca09-e572-55e6-9c7f-bc94a914bffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482301}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482226} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf4268c8-502e-5529-b80f-13d26b351b38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d66735c3-ba98-5f1c-8e1d-7d80133c59cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-335266" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=9y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=9x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2379b8ac-5990-5a88-876d-7a3b13ce4148" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482645}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482629 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09fc895b-be35-574c-a0f1-d2e9dbdc5824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481790} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed34351-e7a9-51f4-906b-adec1b5a834b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of the determinant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481812} {:answer/id #uuid "96028a64-5f62-51b8-b0ec-6376058e920e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482128} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b37ee0-60b6-54bb-88d3-5a9b8ced5669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of a solution curve" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482283}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481790} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1a9e2c-69c2-57dc-98a4-cfafabe3fc1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482403} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7155f794-f353-5a0c-8911-a1f285b25e19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "computing $det({Φ}_{0}(0))$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482037} {:answer/id #uuid "820a69e5-51c6-5ddf-9a50-13e477a4befa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482074} {:answer/id #uuid "8b33370f-a59f-59ec-a300-6d743e8570be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482100} {:answer/id #uuid "e9aa91ff-5e69-576a-ba8f-43568cbef52e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule to ${Φ}_{0}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482333}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482100} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d8bd8e-b3aa-594c-88a8-b125c8eb1696" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482405} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11948125-54a4-5bb6-9128-a9f6fecd3d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "replacing ${Φ}_{0}(0)$ with ${I}_{n}$ in $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481821} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b3c268-1dd4-5950-ab2e-09770223774b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482318} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e2076e-2a67-59cb-8006-dae1d2be288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482320} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f930bb-5307-59dd-80a7-b9bdb0cade2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "integrating $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482321}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481821} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6570167-3f96-5d88-b259-3613309f60d1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1163c64f-8eb6-5387-bd44-2f1d21a98032" :question/math-academy-id "q-336479" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ is obtained from the defining initial value problem for ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ The standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is defined as the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nThe second condition, ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},$ is exactly line $\\text{L4}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ is obtained from the defining initial value problem for ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ by $\\text{using the initial condition }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Replacing ${Φ}_{0}(0)$ with ${I}_{n}$ in the equation $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{replacing }{Φ}_{0}(0)\\text{ with }{I}_{n}\\text{ in }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$"} :step/id #uuid "28f5bdee-7eed-595c-9820-abd9f0486f9a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482640}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482640 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482614 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61796693-027e-5e34-ac41-7245117c63ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the definition of the matrix exponential" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481998} {:answer/id #uuid "67302da8-f87a-5742-b68d-b6432fc52247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the identity ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{XY}$ for matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482012} {:answer/id #uuid "aecba564-d67f-5fda-a785-7112b2e9e6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482187} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad0248d-955a-5ee8-87b5-a6a9266226fa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482409} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba11d7e-2a61-553a-9f1e-d3dc6f191266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481924} {:answer/id #uuid "887d453d-74c3-5783-9f8d-da874648d69f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}=I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482090} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd63aad-1f80-570f-9351-385e1f17ff12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{A{t}_{0}}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}=-I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482144}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481924} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f300979-2c03-5bca-8541-1101107fdf73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482463} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16aae11e-7722-5d5d-a3ff-56d6a8a48158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating line $\\text{L3}$ at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481838} {:answer/id #uuid "1edc9f2b-095b-537f-8b55-2d74f8563acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481858} {:answer/id #uuid "619ca3f7-48eb-583d-ab51-495c74c6bef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying line $\\text{L3}$ on the right by ${e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481858} :answer-field/id #uuid "b775a29d-3fe5-5512-9ef6-783e154724b1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f598b188-bddf-5e21-881f-0c355a5c9889" :question/math-academy-id "q-337119" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L6}$ by\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Line $\\text{L5}$ gives\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c.\n$$\n\nSince $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={I}_{n}$, the right-hand side simplifies to $c$, so\n\n$$\nc=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nSimplify once, then apply $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$, to obtain\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L6}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L6}$, and $\\text{L7}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nUsing $\\text{L6}$, we substitute $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can combine the exponentials:\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7}$ gives line $\\text{L8}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by $\\text{the fact that }{e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$"} :step/id #uuid "7f8b56f9-e657-5fae-8f23-51af234be7a5"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482645 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0f7256d-2d29-5c85-9d4b-72a842efcbc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\cos(6(t-3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482307} :answer-field/id #uuid "199ebf62-577b-5ccf-9a87-eb53b5ca9e94" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482391} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1cf21ed-005b-59e4-9bd4-7e59ab89d886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin(6(t-3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482236}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482236} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cf580ea-9ff4-59fc-a20f-31f6a8ae4bf6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b5cac624-fcaa-5546-985b-94ad2df95205" :question/math-academy-id "q-335436" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-6x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(3) \\\\ y(3)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "% Explanation\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-3)}\\,x(3) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6(t-3))\\, \\\\ \\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(t-3))\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b0d055da-4dd2-51f2-ae55-dae45284bf27" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482648}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482648 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59d8cb4f-ee06-5141-9f71-0005f275d41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481984} {:answer/id #uuid "65ee1f50-cf6b-58b8-afd8-663783704016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482010} {:answer/id #uuid "7e285e86-01d4-53c2-bae8-84c094816e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482063} {:answer/id #uuid "d4207d80-a6eb-5165-8ab9-aace8ee2daa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482281} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c4b7e3-8500-59d1-966d-52216ee1c994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482291}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482291} :answer-field/id #uuid "283ab639-7505-5578-b135-707cc7103815" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8b9edfd9-1c2b-58af-aab6-8f8f25829073" :question/math-academy-id "q-335447" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=6x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(3) \\\\ y(3)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-3)}\\,x(3) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c1447d08-16ad-539a-8ebf-f17fc52a738b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482629}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481767}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506615} :activity/id #uuid "6fa36af2-6f1b-58e0-aae4-87fdba06bbc7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506610 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d4b157-bf69-5bf7-9aad-3eba516db410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}(7t)-3\\operatorname{sin}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309947} {:answer/id #uuid "979f156d-01a6-59f8-8aca-1c984d058959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\cos(7t)-3\\sin(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506174}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506174} :answer-field/id #uuid "334b3886-7b34-5ba0-9e2a-91b524ea209a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edb27977-979e-5d5d-9ca0-7fdf66c63c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}(7t)+3\\operatorname{cos}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310639} {:answer/id #uuid "2678d709-b8ee-55e1-bb84-a652beb39148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\sin(7t)+3\\cos(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505975}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505975} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b7d71a-ace4-5436-8715-dcb69e35eeb8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "085673d9-6167-5c0c-b43c-bc1e085569fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-335262" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\, \\\\ \\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1b4443f1-0280-5047-9471-acc341316636" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506640}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506614 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "942a629e-94b8-5c24-bbcc-97e7d789cb40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391588} {:answer/id #uuid "9b04c091-3bbb-5dae-9ed9-1a467ab29d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391589} {:answer/id #uuid "07f2c784-653a-5833-9229-3fb331cf19a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391590} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea30351-9279-59bc-8f85-f17f0652612d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391591} {:answer/id #uuid "150d70c1-d912-530b-b05b-4c87bea0ff00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391592}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391592} :answer-field/id #uuid "36126579-e63c-590b-a6f7-f58bde2b64a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6580aa1b-3c6f-5533-9e32-e7afb350be95" :question/math-academy-id "q-335450" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(-1) \\\\ y(-1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-(-1))}\\,x(-1) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "27866c4a-22d7-5b58-972c-cfe8b9d40b47" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506617}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506615 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4386227a-d159-5ea7-b586-57eb8ba8b3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309258} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0f7ff2-63f3-536e-a712-0b2b5f23cf38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sin(5t)+\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506276}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506276} :answer-field/id #uuid "53651861-1195-570e-a314-53031aadafea" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17eab3e0-25a6-5d97-ab26-3bfb684afa0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(5t)-3\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308938} {:answer/id #uuid "2633b2d1-98e4-54f9-bd3d-9d6754122e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\cos(5t)+\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505974} :answer-field/id #uuid "d170c52a-07fe-5c77-8bee-10ab3fcdbfb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "622243a2-b3f9-5f58-9668-ac4d025f3264" :question/math-academy-id "q-335260" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\, \\\\ \\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2c32e12b-7fa9-5de5-ab65-67b39782d31e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506610}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506617 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17966dd8-73ff-5dae-a604-448905e652ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "by substituting $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308934} {:answer/id #uuid "6427f8ed-49bc-5e1b-ad8d-b32b63aa2584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "by substitution from line $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309517} {:answer/id #uuid "fc75620b-35c9-591c-aade-7daa879c2824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using the fact that ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310766}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308934} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f5ad037-aae6-5cab-bcba-d870b9717a79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3586d768-5a6b-55e3-b74b-d7384ddf8b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309155} {:answer/id #uuid "96845e88-24f3-523a-aa89-8c99b1e81691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At}$ for any matrix $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309954} {:answer/id #uuid "9af374b3-6d71-58a8-b886-dbe3e18d9a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310003}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309155} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7d8c45-9baf-5f3c-9730-e684d4f25418" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b4f6d50-4cc2-5464-88dd-148342d77dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309204} {:answer/id #uuid "757e14df-a5bc-5543-aecf-5b5c92b609a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{A{t}_{0}}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}=I{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309664} {:answer/id #uuid "b7846f39-941e-5fc0-a5af-9df9b5d9178c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A{t}_{0}}I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309204} :answer-field/id #uuid "e445eb61-c230-53f6-a72a-4588c5fa0f2d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "45874040-9e7b-5fb5-9a00-ef344d9b3cd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337109" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$  Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Starting from $\\text{L3},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe evaluate both sides at $t={t}_{0}$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L4}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ $\\text{by substituting }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Line $\\text{L5}$ gives\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c.\n$$\n\nSince $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={I}_{n}$, the right-hand side simplifies to $c$, so\n\n$$\nc=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nSimplify once, then apply $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$, to obtain\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L6}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$"} :step/id #uuid "323902b1-2dc9-5b75-a6de-c749bb49c955"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506640 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77290e62-6148-5a0c-a377-bec8579eec5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309679} {:answer/id #uuid "97fc3697-404e-5fb0-854e-fc0c8ff7d45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2t{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309968} {:answer/id #uuid "9a02425e-0f01-5418-94f2-288ad58f1b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309988} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c51a8a-3c2a-5bdb-a554-d4a1fb8e8ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310100} {:answer/id #uuid "d266e8d7-9b0b-5943-9acc-ac02de0e98d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310440}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310440} :answer-field/id #uuid "a01f0c87-7802-5bf3-a753-2547be1ae761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "62010a37-a91d-55bc-8c8e-6361d12d6c44" :question/math-academy-id "q-335267" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9b0fd3c3-6109-5d52-8875-92b52299b80a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506614}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505906}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535137} :activity/id #uuid "cbc6fbed-6e86-5dc3-b2c1-9930dc5f3f8a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535092 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311561 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475bc880-3247-5ccb-b66d-eadc8b060abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309293} {:answer/id #uuid "49f14ac6-ae6a-52fb-ac47-59a4da45cbf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -7\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309314} {:answer/id #uuid "dddc0c7d-92d4-5f6a-896b-0827b4812b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310526} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ce61e9-90fc-5364-9639-0f81ce141cae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310567} {:answer/id #uuid "edf565d5-c17e-5fec-b7c6-a3893ad155fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310642}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310526} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3f0017-0fc8-57f5-b880-e66a5a5ec724" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0363c023-46f1-587f-a57b-04e2d2812056" :question/math-academy-id "q-335265" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "01dd852f-2929-5c79-b2c7-9966a69ca50b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535096}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535096 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68733ae1-b610-5dd9-b95d-12135f00648e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos(5(t+2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534477}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534477} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e339ad0-7370-56ee-a106-ae32b1e3a838" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4db09dc0-d4c5-5e09-a70f-eae2e3269be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin(5(t+2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534416}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534416} :answer-field/id #uuid "b890faf2-939e-5590-92f1-af9dc867356d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "530f8a57-b248-5ddf-8ae9-a8b808f3a729" :question/math-academy-id "q-335435" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-2) \\\\ y(-2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"130px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+2)}\\,x(-2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2)) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2))\\, \\\\ \\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1241689c-e056-52b5-b26f-3355c23157a3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535127}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535115 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229697 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c14b0b-6134-5bed-bee6-816912d61365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{Mt}{e}^{-M{t}_{0}}={e}^{M(t-{t}_{0})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308890} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4b7b03-dd23-5804-b0ab-e36a1cf3ccf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309700} {:answer/id #uuid "9916cee6-3a2c-57ad-bb9b-91e60a976e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At}$ for any matrix $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309982} {:answer/id #uuid "db7e796b-5ae4-519f-a67a-d1aed48231c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$Bt-B{t}_{0}=B(t-{t}_{0})$ for any $t$ and ${t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310506}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309700} :answer-field/id #uuid "543d5358-872d-5528-9c7f-c8cc3db9937c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217f2965-3def-569f-947d-692f1650809e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "by substitution from line $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309001} {:answer/id #uuid "667b7e3d-b549-5061-a30e-feb651e43fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "by substituting $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309536} {:answer/id #uuid "dbbe8906-11f6-5f0e-8be5-7e60e92604ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using the fact that ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310508}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309536} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e482e3-780a-5e91-b090-efa6a61b43ee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311264} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "470e1341-576f-51bf-8372-83789f8096ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the definition of matrix exponential" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309291} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc59270-51b2-5c62-b938-b48c9f3532b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "the properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310038} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fb24cf-f960-5624-9b68-8fb29c368dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310437}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310038} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2f5da27-dc12-5c0e-8352-c31ac3b14b77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "da9645d1-ab1f-59b5-93f4-27c23f00e120" :question/math-academy-id "q-336639" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ is true by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ is true by $\\text{the properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Starting from $\\text{L3},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe evaluate both sides at $t={t}_{0}$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L4}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ $\\text{by substituting }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$"} :step/id #uuid "94ec5f0a-352f-5ac0-bc02-f9deb9d28d5c"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535127 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c34b001-8f8c-572c-b23f-54c9b0c5e906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308966} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf1caf8-52d6-5aa2-81ff-73de1341e51f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ at $t=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309083} {:answer/id #uuid "487cf069-3ce8-55d6-8f31-00a5f9dc3430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "computing $det({Φ}_{0}(0))$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309301} {:answer/id #uuid "8b861976-a2d2-5456-8f84-3e614119c072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule to ${Φ}_{0}(0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309850}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308966} :answer-field/id #uuid "746ca404-3ff2-5606-b348-9000ebf3fa87" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "013fe3e7-48a3-5036-84c8-ff7674a40c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308751} {:answer/id #uuid "05b6b3d7-e359-543e-a6f7-70fbe1665e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308794} {:answer/id #uuid "77824231-14d3-5fd4-a1b5-159f6745b22b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309685} {:answer/id #uuid "b90dcf6d-1547-5a3f-9184-7b3f3f7726d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310248}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309685} :answer-field/id #uuid "875aa7e2-b4fd-5e3f-9e1e-8e2d7af33a25" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311175} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351e9093-98d5-59b5-baff-6bad3f2b3811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309152} {:answer/id #uuid "50102d24-a6a9-5c87-aa99-704cb37623ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309355} {:answer/id #uuid "adde2792-5c0e-5b9b-9cec-0d10e61be9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of the determinant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310155} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe97a2c-08be-5a21-a27a-cc283819bfcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of a solution curve" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310271}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309355} :answer-field/id #uuid "93fd95bd-02de-51a7-9380-23ea3323f2a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9684981a-5306-5edd-b5f3-7d483bf8c5e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-336481" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ By definition, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ satisfies the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nThe second condition here is exactly line $\\text{L4},$ so $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by $\\text{using the initial condition }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$"} :step/id #uuid "c7e18732-59fb-5584-9670-78b1b3e4c537" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535115}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535137 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2826f3b3-aa19-5166-9709-c29a10e19d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534348} {:answer/id #uuid "4c00ea3b-3ce4-5e0c-8832-b95dc6c0a81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534412} {:answer/id #uuid "5075de84-7cd8-5fc4-90bb-1cd990dbc9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534423} {:answer/id #uuid "70233942-007a-5043-b53a-395ec3709d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534501} {:answer/id #uuid "c1df0fbb-0a33-5bd3-9288-292dffd71dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534698}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534501} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3c1b24-93bd-5251-bf4f-c0926f7bb2fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4ca0dd99-a2aa-57ba-b99d-effa4b0eacfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-333981" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "df50ea20-ddc6-5750-beca-6ed839b9bdcd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535092}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534261}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542244} :activity/id #uuid "ef3a3edc-d7d1-547d-8515-08949bf0a91c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542244 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bfd4a6b-0cff-5025-ac15-1ba07589a334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541606}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541606} :answer-field/id #uuid "c00aedbd-3d32-591a-9238-e662e5a71296" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d6d80b-bee2-5ffe-978c-9a216b9c3522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541538}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541538} :answer-field/id #uuid "7397605e-8fc4-5376-8bac-4c5dbc127439" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77f295d1-1cbb-5b17-a7ef-414238a16c0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334547" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(1) \\\\ y(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{2(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,{e}^{2(t-1)}\\, \\\\ \\,0\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2ec118fb-8e61-556c-8854-cbf857a4c88b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542273}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542252 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "911a0b91-8cfc-5c90-8612-d186b86260d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372705} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7b866a-6af6-5c53-8767-9d73d4a5a6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372706} {:answer/id #uuid "f59f7b97-72d7-544d-92fb-affc25bc255f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372707} {:answer/id #uuid "fba88690-6a3e-517e-b451-20f63869feb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372708} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e0b67b-92e9-576c-93cc-05727469679d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372709}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372706} :answer-field/id #uuid "1879bd9d-054e-59da-ab7b-0aabcf601f7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "981edc7d-4bd0-566a-a596-3fb1014b4ef7" :question/math-academy-id "q-335264" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "488b9d3b-a97f-5cfc-9ee9-56aee87c9e33" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542272}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542267 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372710 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d581ab-eac2-55b5-888d-deaf7a002aed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using properties of $det({Φ}_{0}(0))$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372712} {:answer/id #uuid "813ef154-d604-561e-b48e-0b35325f3927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372713} {:answer/id #uuid "fdaf11ea-4164-580f-829e-d2abaeceb857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372714} {:answer/id #uuid "80ab58cb-932a-566d-b586-c196589d930b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "replacing ${Φ}_{0}(0)$ with ${I}_{n}$ in $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372715}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372715} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4499e16-aabb-5cb2-a67c-ad7557ae05f6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372711} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853ace54-49de-53c0-82ed-cfb835e09e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372717} {:answer/id #uuid "906f3949-ca05-5f13-8b47-f3dce789277e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372718} {:answer/id #uuid "9c8541f4-adab-5b02-9915-46d4efed7ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using diagonalization of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372719} {:answer/id #uuid "167e465a-c594-58b2-a782-69d90ccc3a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372717} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0cfc463-a00c-5a02-b25e-b6454e6a70ed" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "484d762f-5acf-5df4-8df4-94cc90a1d4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372722} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e78e24-6079-5e65-a2d8-6a25635330b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of a solution curve" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372723} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddac18e-8996-5267-a9f1-7a3b6bca18c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "properties of the determinant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372724} {:answer/id #uuid "12142844-889a-5ee2-b9bb-a31bbc51020a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372722} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dea9463-8880-5a50-ac39-82e4de0d8f50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "da2b3537-4a89-5afc-8ad7-721d1c3c30a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-336480" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, any solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ From $\\text{L2}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is precisely line $\\text{L3}.$ Thus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we know\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Replacing ${Φ}_{0}(0)$ with ${I}_{n}$ in the equation $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{replacing }{Φ}_{0}(0)\\text{ with }{I}_{n}\\text{ in }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$"} :step/id #uuid "845477bd-8d9d-58e3-9bf9-2073bbad3f86"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542272 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f8dc2a-d1c1-50ad-9080-e4aea1133091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308761}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308761} :answer-field/id #uuid "93eace97-bb5c-5bd2-b8df-7eca81320545" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07bdd633-a0bf-5ddf-ac96-58b9d4b0f277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308806}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308806} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6cac817-7eaa-5d9c-919e-8afb3c166bfa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "80bead61-fb6c-5bf6-88d2-511e52d01763" :question/math-academy-id "q-335273" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-2)} & (t-2){e}^{3(t-2)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-2)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}\\, \\\\ \\,{e}^{3(t-2)}\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "940a38de-c4fa-51fc-b135-2a4dcc4b60cf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542267}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542273 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359dac84-023f-5ac4-b1e5-2b024191e8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541532} {:answer/id #uuid "557ae54f-10b2-58ab-9e71-0c628ea5f179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541593} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4ad265-f473-5a67-8913-d792566b24af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541815} {:answer/id #uuid "d11ef4d7-b160-5577-b380-46de80da0930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541866} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c0af83-088a-5ec4-9706-445e6d105d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541932}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541932} :answer-field/id #uuid "f94becd7-b475-5661-836a-13b2396bb899" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ebc3a86d-4663-502d-a702-2a2557f07e8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334779" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=8y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-8x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} :step/id #uuid "a176a8d0-ae3d-5337-b4e5-e954a5e68792" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542252}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541425}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555942} :activity/id #uuid "5acdb4c1-3708-5ab3-a633-c96f6a0ca605" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555886 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c48896b-a018-521e-946b-fe65b686effd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555247} {:answer/id #uuid "7a745ab5-2e30-5358-a661-1005ce9fee4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555285} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5a344b-c228-5070-a3de-d96f53cbd405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555331} {:answer/id #uuid "cf972ef6-5de2-58b9-b5d8-6de313e595af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555494} {:answer/id #uuid "da11d876-2fe9-5885-b371-78fffbd4906e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555528}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9bfc61d-9208-5f2a-9171-0d8c90db3cd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "27a5f814-886e-5a61-acf9-facf209e99cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-335263" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1f9dafb5-c34d-5312-911b-4c4907b35329" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555890}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555890 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d2dabb0-502b-562b-b584-741bd2219b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sin(3(t-2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555287} :answer-field/id #uuid "12370503-03e0-554e-be1b-d6e2ad47764c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d71b20dd-cdf6-5315-9b31-8b02be6facce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\cos(3(t-2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555515}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555515} :answer-field/id #uuid "645a6766-29a4-5adf-89b5-f8cdeb82aee5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ea042103-925d-51d6-8c12-93baa97ad8a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335432" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"130px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(t-2)) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(t-2)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(t-2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(t-2))\\, \\\\ \\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(t-2))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "30aafb2e-fb68-534a-be26-1fdfcb35d392" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555910}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555910 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391579 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c3294a-f087-5672-a53e-117506420382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391581} {:answer/id #uuid "601ea9e6-24b0-535e-bb17-49ca178db97e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391582} {:answer/id #uuid "59b758f5-6067-571d-908b-9e50262c9da7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391583} {:answer/id #uuid "66384a82-a5a2-5020-8b9b-8db002bae474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391584} {:answer/id #uuid "70ed0219-7267-5410-9f26-31afb335cb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391585}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391584} :answer-field/id #uuid "afd92e9b-c3b2-5f27-ae61-1167e9f32949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6ab60b60-d1a6-5ef2-aaf8-6579001f22b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335448" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(1) \\\\ y(1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "66b1ba2f-47f6-57cc-9eb4-b3492a919d6a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555927}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555927 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396936 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614d6ab5-5628-5fbe-818a-c13fdda2c28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396938} {:answer/id #uuid "ce094f55-879b-5b96-bedb-c8a97168bac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396939} {:answer/id #uuid "cccff4fe-20c3-5cb7-9681-92cc25121511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396940} {:answer/id #uuid "ab84e7ed-d6a8-520d-8b8d-917218916f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396941}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396939} :answer-field/id #uuid "62e5d724-e4aa-50ec-8d98-2ca352e011f4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3461c8f3-6347-5cda-a1c7-cd2ab24c6c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396943} {:answer/id #uuid "41161c5d-5b28-5637-adb6-191d50f983ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396944} {:answer/id #uuid "411ea3ea-3c55-50ae-abd5-5130b8a1d446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396945} {:answer/id #uuid "a18ae187-4ca1-50ee-ba3f-d6af9219c439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396946}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396944} :answer-field/id #uuid "d10c4b52-29cf-597a-97d0-5df761b842ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396942} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5363f0a4-bc32-5773-a19c-82bd214aee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396948} {:answer/id #uuid "83b75a12-331a-52aa-8a26-b868726772a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396949} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3f9f52-0d94-5534-85e6-03b3ff052905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "using diagonalization of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396950} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e0fc6c-fed0-5c5b-bab5-4daeb2418d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396948} :answer-field/id #uuid "b441f599-459e-58bd-b0d0-12769ed6a804" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b476f440-04ac-55c0-bbfe-8012f8f71f27" :question/math-academy-id "q-336477" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by  {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from $\\text{L2},$ we have the identity\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L3}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}\\text{ into }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$, $\\text{L2},$ $\\text{L5},$ and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L1}$ we have ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At},$ and from $\\text{L5}$ we know $c=x(0).$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ (line $\\text{L2}$), we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$"} :step/id #uuid "b41f67d2-ff2d-5a29-ac2d-303ee9d8158f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555942 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555759 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "280d8127-c31a-5e2e-b9dc-665b3585f060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-9t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555084} {:answer/id #uuid "44c32af4-4f13-53b5-8974-40ae755cae35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{9t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555147} {:answer/id #uuid "48431481-3e8e-57a8-83d2-eb0cb39cf23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555154} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c5ce55-c333-5011-848b-c5650ca56801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555391} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a1cb7e-8b62-5bfd-ab90-3eb838df358f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-9t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555392}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555391} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cd5bc44-1d8a-5b80-a78e-d0c95223991b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "021e3fe3-3d72-56fe-ac1a-be1f9dae2590" :question/math-academy-id "q-335026" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=9y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=9x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} :step/id #uuid "d424c598-a6f1-571f-8fba-0e759c88c86f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555886}}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554993}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046668} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563778} :activity/id #uuid "d79f13d1-043c-58ab-89f2-0282f6144b80" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/id #uuid "8a6eb2f8-5287-523f-8df7-f21c0db8796c" :topic/math-academy-id 6690} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563764 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "246dbb57-80e4-56b7-8e34-27bb9114f64c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563026} {:answer/id #uuid "45cfe9fb-b684-53e4-ab59-2be2f93d9858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563103} {:answer/id #uuid "4bdeeefb-735e-5811-8754-67e744ec5c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563112} {:answer/id #uuid "63a09f8e-7c0b-5249-a0c2-f6b28192c424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563174} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e28dd3-0453-550c-862e-c838b2f1aca0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563408}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563174} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ea9a430-3071-50b8-b617-7ec74f7a4ddc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eaac4ca3-6936-5237-9e98-3d7aa72b5385" :question/math-academy-id "q-335025" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} :step/id #uuid "0b859571-5266-5412-bce5-e8cf5c6397c7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563785}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563778 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa2879fd-b388-54d3-91a6-9889b3cc921c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402115} {:answer/id #uuid "7f291e69-4dda-53a6-8a62-f0061587ecc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402116} {:answer/id #uuid "8c43d172-267c-5edc-a00c-eb37c3afc069" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402117} {:answer/id #uuid "6160111a-8bd8-53b3-8c8a-0ec9830b724b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402118} {:answer/id #uuid "a82130d9-20ec-5094-9c98-83b539f3238e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402119}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402117} :answer-field/id #uuid "d370b658-9d56-5718-913a-a06cb231e944" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402114}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3c065292-5916-5335-a2ce-48232ddb8e4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-333856" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} :step/id #uuid "3c2b1be3-b138-5354-826d-0d722fe6ba4e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563791}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563785 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311562 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dcee7af-7056-5b97-9372-e26001db1e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309094} {:answer/id #uuid "54b88482-9a48-53c8-b436-71c2a5fcea44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309389} {:answer/id #uuid "6b578480-7196-5ccc-b193-d86e5994a039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309581} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a02da3-4c0e-59a8-9ef3-fc732675a0bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{-6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310315} {:answer/id #uuid "c60df48c-c6c5-573d-a4c8-6c244c51b408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4t{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310339}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309389} :answer-field/id #uuid "84cab197-81f5-503d-a0d6-83d5086f95b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "32bd0c44-4a18-5100-9555-27f58f065186" :question/math-academy-id "q-335268" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=6x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=6y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "66628ba8-6a25-551d-82f3-4c8835969083" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563803}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563791 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3c6cf5-b1b3-57df-abab-56efb96d89f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}e^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228209} {:answer/id #uuid "a0710c2c-0243-5683-af7c-dd5379117712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228210} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fa826d-432e-567c-b648-b350c15d4141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix}e^{4t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228211} {:answer/id #uuid "02570066-a4ba-5ed7-9532-5cfdb98488c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228212} {:answer/id #uuid "310ab06b-a4b2-54bf-bfab-dcc138d0d2d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228213}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6e4f9160-e954-5fed-b512-345d3c9abd75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be54f80-3e00-5c60-8d2c-859b73f1b04a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402121} {:answer/id #uuid "a489112a-2e25-5139-8701-0da71be4eaed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402122} {:answer/id #uuid "f40839a9-1ee4-555c-b0e0-836cd8ef8a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402123} {:answer/id #uuid "d13024ed-e948-5192-b456-f8fc65a79957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402124} {:answer/id #uuid "2d239718-30d6-534b-aa0f-8cec27c7ffe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402125}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402125} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbee732a-a84c-5f81-aebe-d7513334919d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "783e954f-0aef-53d9-a6ee-3a8685affb71" :question/math-academy-id "q-334772" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} :step/id #uuid "8d6857f9-1674-50e2-bd6e-08e1076f3091" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563764}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563803 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3e6f6d2-ce35-5cb0-a6c5-f9b0db8f35b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sin(4(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563409}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563409} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f7c85fb-7d21-5d48-8f24-4c37d6bc47ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8ac02a8-cb92-5cdb-baec-1e8c677c1a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\cos(4(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563502}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563502} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ff392b1-754b-5f5c-ad8a-af1f4c91dfa9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "701145a1-1f00-509b-9c1b-60626233c2a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-335434" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(1) \\\\ y(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"130px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-1))\\, \\\\ \\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-1))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cd08637e-a1a7-546e-8e76-ea7112573f7e"}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562936}]}
